  "notes": "The set of friends and qualifying transactions is only known at runtime, so the problem uses a representative instance: two friend contacts (friend-1, friend-2) and three received transactions (txn-1, txn-2 from friend-1; txn-3 from friend-2). Transactions and the comment are declared as domain constants so supervisor-complete-task can list every goal condition in its precondition without parameters; apps are also constants and are therefore not redeclared in the problem objects. supervisor.show_profile supplies the login usernames (phone number for phone, email for venmo). phone.search_contacts with query/relationship 'friend' makes (friends-found) true, which unlocks the static friend-email facts; phone.get_current_date_and_time establishes the window start date (today - 6 days = 2023-05-26, so the window includes today and the previous 6 days). venmo.show_transactions is called once per friend with user_email, min_created_at and direction='received' and makes (transactions-found ?p) true, unlocking the transactions received from that friend. Each qualifying transaction must then be liked and commented 'Thanks!' (both actions carry a non-API person parameter to tie them to the lookup). The unused query/relationship/direction parameters are single-valued objects that just carry the literal API arguments. Only like_count changes on transactions and no other records change, matching the evaluation.",
